# Generated by ./gradlew :featuregen:kplusplusSync
/krapped/*

# ...except the discovered-instantiation manifest, which IS committed (issue #25).
#
# The SYNC_REQUIRED manifest is grown lazily over compile passes: the FIR plugin
# only learns it needs a NESTED generic (e.g. std::vector<std::vector<int>>) once
# the inner binding (std::vector<int>) has been generated and compiled against. A
# cold krapped/ therefore needed several sync->compile->sync cycles to reach the
# full closure — a fresh worktree / CI checkout looked like a failure on first run.
#
# Committing the converged manifest pins that closure as a deterministic, version-
# controlled input: a cold checkout now starts with the whole SYNC_REQUIRED set, so
# a single `:featuregen:nativeTest` generates everything up front and converges in
# one pass. Everything else under krapped/ (generated src, the .def, generated.txt,
# fixups.json) stays machine-generated and ignored. When a new test introduces a
# new instantiation, the FIR plugin appends it here on the next build; commit the
# updated manifest so cold starts stay single-pass.
!/krapped/requested.txt
